        {
          "id": 2687528132,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "No, the mask is 0x01ff, so 1 bit from the first byte and all of the next.\n\nWe don't usually flag cases where the call is for less data than the width of the field, but I added a check for where there is an explicit mask and the call is less than the width of its bits.  It could still be better, e.g., a mask of 0x0ff0 needs a length of 2.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
